==Reign ({{abbr|2443|2029.46 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}–present)==
{{Main|Qodzarian era}}

After being enthroned, Qodzar dismissed several [[Royal Ministers of Qym|Royal Ministers]] of his father's government, while retaining others. Among the retained ministers were [[Lord Moqi of Zhifol|Lord Moqi]], the [[Royal Ministry of Public Safety (Qym)|Royal Minister of Public Safety]]; [[Lord Gozaq of Zhifol|Lord Gozaq]], the [[Royal Ministry of Defense (Qym)|Royal Minister of Defense]]; his uncle [[Prince Nimerk of Qym|Prince Nimerk]], the [[Royal Ministry of Finance (Qym)|Royal Minister of Finance]]; [[Lord Otagost of Zhifol|Lord Otagost]], the [[Royal Ministry of Intergovernmental Affairs (Qym)|Royal Minister of Intergovernmental Affairs]]; his aunt [[Princess Snegada of Qym|Princess Snegada]], the [[Royal Ministry of Health (Qym)|Royal Minister of Health]]; his father's cousin [[Princess Bozhisha of Qym|Princess Bozhisha]], the [[Royal Ministry of Labor (Qym)|Royal Minister of Labor]]; and his aunt [[Princess Navesh of Qym|Princess Navesh]], the [[Royal Ministry of Education and Research (Qym)|Royal Minister of Education and Research]]. 

As part of [[Government of Qym#Current members|his new government]], Qodzar appointed his older sister [[Princess Myril of Qym|Princess Myril]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Culture and Tourism (Qym)|Royal Minister of Culture and Tourism]], and his younger sister [[Princess Tëdozha of Qym|Princess Tëdozha]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Justice (Qym)|Royal Minister of Justice]]. Furthermore, he appointed [[Lord Donadar of Zhifol|Lord Donadar]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Trade and Industry (Qym)|Royal Minister of Trade and Industry]], [[Lady Vjesmica of Zhifol|Lady Vjesmica]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Energy (Qym)|Royal Minister of Energy]], his second cousin, [[Princess Anavi of Qym|Princess Anavi]], as the [[Royal Ministry of Nutrition (Qym)|Royal Minister of Nutrition]], [[Lord Martek of Zhifol|Lord Martek]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Transport (Qym)|Royal Minister of Transport]], [[Lord Sumir of Zhifol|Lord Sumir]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Natural Resources (Qym)|Royal Minister of Natural Resources]], [[Lord Ratijzy of Zhifol|Lord Ratijzy]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Housing and National Development (Qym)|Royal Minister of Housing and National Development]], and [[Lady Nezha of Zhifol|Lady Nezha]] as the [[Royal Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Qym)|Royal Minister of Foreign Affairs]].

